I have enough to answer. The one clearly faulty service is ts-admin-user-service, and its effect reaches the user through ts-ui-dashboard.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-admin-user-service",
      "fault_kind": "application_method_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT 'ab' p, service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind k, count(*) n, round(approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.95),1) p95 FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-admin-user-service' AND span_name IN ('AdminUserController.getAllUsers','GET /api/v1/adminuserservice/users') GROUP BY ALL UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*), round(approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.95),1) FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-admin-user-service' AND span_name IN ('AdminUserController.getAllUsers','GET /api/v1/adminuserservice/users') GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "getAllUsers p95 rose from about 8 ms to about 1,655 ms; its GET /users server span rose from 11 ms to 1,657 ms."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT trace_id, service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, round(duration/1e6,1) ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE trace_id='97ce44276c8fe878b3682965b56f61a6' ORDER BY time",
          "claim": "In a slow trace, getAllUsers self-time is about 1,640 ms while its only child GET call takes about 8 ms."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT metric, service_name, round(avg(value),3) av FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE service_name='ts-admin-user-service' AND metric IN ('k8s.pod.cpu.usage','k8s.pod.memory.working_set') GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Pod CPU (about 0.01 cores) and memory (about 467 MB) are low, so the slowdown is not container resource exhaustion."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "ts-admin-user-service",
      "to": "ts-ui-dashboard",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT 'ab' p, service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind k, count(*) n, round(approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.95),1) p95 FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name='GET /api/v1/adminuserservice/users' AND attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY ALL UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*), round(approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.95),1) FROM normal_traces WHERE span_name='GET /api/v1/adminuserservice/users' AND attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "ui-dashboard's GET /api/v1/adminuserservice/users server p95 rose from 13 ms to about 1,663 ms, matching the admin-user slowdown."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```
